---
// /promise/ — the standing promise the whole line is held to, written for
// Flow first (the flagship since 2026-08-27), then Relay and Arena.
//
// History: born as the Relay D5 ask (2026-07-01): buyer-based gating +
// never-regress. Rewritten 2026-08-29 on the operator's direction to be
// cross-product with Flow in front. The Flow facts come from the constants the
// pricing surface already enforces (src/data/flow-pricing.ts: FLOW_PROMISE,
// FLOW_LAPSE_FACTS, FLOW_WITHDRAWAL_NOTICE) and from the product lane's shipped
// Flow Guide wording (flow-growth ledger 2026-08-29 08:05: "see, switch off, or
// whose outcome you control"). The Relay facts are the D5 entry. The Arena
// facts are the ones /arena/ already states. Prices never appear as literals.
// Voice: grade 3-5, jargon explained, no em-dashes (website-copy-style).
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import SectionLabel from '../components/ui/SectionLabel.astro';
import { SITE, PUBLISHER } from '../data/seo';
import { ogMeta } from '../data/og';
import { FLOW, formatUsd } from '../data/commerce.ts';
import { FLOW_PROMISE, FLOW_LAPSE_FACTS, FLOW_WITHDRAWAL_NOTICE } from '../data/flow-pricing.ts';
import { ORIONFOLD_FLOW_LIVE } from '../data/launch.ts';

const og = ogMeta('/promise/');

const PROMISE_DESCRIPTION =
  'The Orionfold promise across Flow, Relay and Arena: what is free stays free, what you own keeps working on your own machine, and you pay for the AI, the content or the upkeep, never for the right to use what is yours.';

const flowPlanSentence = ORIONFOLD_FLOW_LIVE
  ? `Flow Pro is ${formatUsd(FLOW.monthly.amount)} a month or ${formatUsd(FLOW.annual.amount)} a year, and every install starts with 10 Pro Days.`
  : 'Flow Pro is the subscription; every install starts with 10 Pro Days.';

// The three ideas that make up the promise, stated plainly up top.
const summaryCards = [
  {
    title: 'Free stays free',
    body: 'Flow Base, which is reading, writing, searching, organizing and exporting your documents, is free forever. Relay Core and direct use are free. Anything that ever shipped free does not later become paid.',
  },
  {
    title: 'You pay for the work, not the right',
    body: 'Flow Pro is the AI doing work: proposing changes, drawing charts, routing models. A Relay Pack is maintained content. An Arena Field Edition license is a proven, receipted year of a lab. None of them is a key to something you already had.',
  },
  {
    title: 'What you own keeps working',
    body: 'Licenses are checked on your own machine. A lapsed Flow plan leaves every document open and editable. Installed Relay packs keep running. An Arena box keeps running with your data on it.',
  },
];

// The standing test, expanded, product by product. Flow first.
const sections = [
  {
    title: 'Flow: your documents are free forever. The AI is what you pay for.',
    paragraphs: [
      `That sentence is the whole Flow deal, and the app enforces it: ${FLOW_PROMISE}`,
      'Flow Base has no trial, no expiry, no account and nothing to buy. You can read, write, search, organize and export plain Markdown files in your own folders for as long as you like. You can also read every receipt, timeline and evidence score the AI ever produced, free, forever.',
      `If a model runs, it is part of the subscription. Proofreading, rewriting, drawing charts and diagrams from your text, and routing work to local or cloud models are Flow Pro. ${flowPlanSentence} One license covers one person on their own Macs.`,
      `When a plan ends, Flow says one thing, only when you ask its AI to run: “${FLOW_WITHDRAWAL_NOTICE}” Here is what a lapse does not do, each line enforced in the app rather than promised on a page:`,
    ],
    bullets: FLOW_LAPSE_FACTS,
    after: 'Your license is checked on your Mac. Flow does not need a connection to use it, and it never has to check in with us to keep working.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Relay: the engine is free, the packs are the content',
    paragraphs: [
      'Relay Core, direct Cells, installers, schedulers and the public Cell image ship free for everyone. There is no tier that turns the free engine into a working product; direct use is complete on its own.',
      'A Pack license unlocks the premium packs you own and keeps them current: ready-made agents, blueprints and setups we maintain for you. You are buying the upkeep, not the ability to run it. A separate Relay Host license covers managed customer Cells within its signed capacity and never makes the free path a trial.',
      'Here is a real example of free staying free. While building the first paid pack, the Agency pack, we found the engine was missing two things: packs could not add their own triggers, and blueprints could not be scheduled. We shipped both free, for every user, in the same release that put the paid pack on sale.',
      'If a Pack license lapses, everything you installed keeps working exactly as it did; renewal is only about the year’s new and updated packs and priority support. If a Host term ends, running Cells keep running and export and recovery stay available; new managed capacity, forward paid updates and re-download stop, and compatible critical-security fixes remain included.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Arena: a proven year, on a box you own',
    paragraphs: [
      'Arena Field Edition turns the NVIDIA DGX Spark you own into a private AI lab. It installs in one pass, proves itself on first boot with a verifiable receipt you can read, and the twelve-month window re-gates and re-receipts the box so it stays proven.',
      'The box is yours, your data is on it, and your license works offline. If Orionfold went away tomorrow, your lab keeps running. Every release ships with a signed record of where it came from and a full parts list, and the install is checked against a fingerprint before it runs.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'What we will never do',
    paragraphs: [
      'So the promise is concrete, here are the things we have decided against, on purpose, for every product:',
    ],
    bullets: [
      'No database licensing. Your right to use what you own is not a row we can flip off.',
      'No nag banners. Relay’s command-line tools never advertise. Flow tells you one thing, only at the moment you ask its AI to run without a plan, and your documents stay open and editable either way.',
      'No online re-validation. The license is checked on your machine; your software never sends your data to Orionfold, and it never has to check in with us to keep working. Flow reaches the network only for things you can see, switch off, or whose outcome you control: checking for updates, the models and providers you add, and the Guide when you ask. As of Flow 1.5.5 it keeps no usage statistics and sends no crash reports. If a future Flow offers to share counts or crash reports, it will be a switch that starts off, with every field listed.',
      'No expiry that disables what you installed. A lapsed Flow plan leaves every document open. Installed Relay packs keep running. An Arena box keeps running.',
    ],
  },
];
---
<Layout
  title="Our promise: what you pay for, and what you never lose · Orionfold"
  description={PROMISE_DESCRIPTION}
  ogImage={og.image}
  ogImageAlt={og.alt}
  jsonLd={[
    {
      '@context': 'https://schema.org',
      '@type': 'WebPage',
      name: 'Our promise · Orionfold',
      url: `${SITE.url}/promise/`,
      inLanguage: 'en',
      publisher: PUBLISHER,
      description: PROMISE_DESCRIPTION,
    },
    {
      '@context': 'https://schema.org',
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: SITE.url },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Promise', item: `${SITE.url}/promise/` },
      ],
    },
  ]}
>
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <section class="relative overflow-hidden px-6 pt-32 pb-18">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none">
        <div class="absolute left-1/2 top-14 h-[26rem] w-[26rem] -translate-x-1/2 rounded-full bg-primary/[0.10] blur-[150px]"></div>
        <div class="absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 h-40" style="background: linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent, var(--color-surface-raised));"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="relative z-10 mx-auto max-w-5xl">
        <div data-animate>
          <SectionLabel text="Our promise" />
        </div>
        <div class="mt-5 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.2fr)_18rem] lg:items-end">
          <div>
            <h1 data-animate class="font-display text-[clamp(2.2rem,6vw,4.5rem)] leading-[1.02]" style="transition-delay: 80ms">
              What you pay for, and what you never lose.
            </h1>
            <p data-animate class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-muted" style="transition-delay: 160ms">
              Flow, Relay and Arena are built on one rule. The part you run is free or yours for good. The part you pay for is the AI’s work, maintained content, or a proven year of upkeep. Anything that ships free stays free, and nothing you own ever has to call home to keep working. This page is the standing promise we hold every product to.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div data-animate class="rounded-2xl border border-primary/30 bg-primary/[0.06] p-5 shadow-[0_20px_80px_-40px_rgba(0,0,0,0.75)]" style="transition-delay: 220ms">
            <p class="font-mono text-[0.62rem] uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-primary/70">The short version</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-text">
              Free stays free. What you own keeps working on your own machine. You pay for the AI, the content or the upkeep, never for the right to use what is yours.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-y border-border bg-surface-raised px-6 py-10">
      <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-4 md:grid-cols-3" data-animate-stagger>
        {summaryCards.map((card) => (
          <article data-animate class="rounded-2xl border border-border/70 bg-surface/80 p-5">
            <p class="font-mono text-[0.6rem] uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-primary">{card.title}</p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">{card.body}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="px-6 py-18">
      <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-6 lg:grid-cols-[15rem_minmax(0,1fr)]">
        <aside data-animate class="lg:sticky lg:top-28 h-fit rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface-raised/70 p-5">
          <p class="font-mono text-[0.62rem] uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-text-dim">Why this is written down</p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
            A promise you cannot point to is not a promise. So we put ours on a page, in plain words, and hold every product to it. If we ever break it, you have this to hold us to.
          </p>
        </aside>

        <div class="space-y-5" data-animate-stagger>
          {sections.map((section) => (
            <section data-animate class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface-raised/70 p-6 sm:p-8">
              <h2 class="text-2xl">{section.title}</h2>
              <div class="mt-4 space-y-4">
                {section.paragraphs.map((paragraph) => (
                  <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-muted">{paragraph}</p>
                ))}
                {section.bullets && (
                  <ul class="space-y-3 pt-2">
                    {section.bullets.map((bullet) => (
                      <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
                        <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
                        <span>{bullet}</span>
                      </li>
                    ))}
                  </ul>
                )}
                {section.after && (
                  <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-muted">{section.after}</p>
                )}
              </div>
            </section>
          ))}

          <div data-animate class="rounded-2xl border border-primary/30 bg-primary/[0.06] p-6 sm:p-8">
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text">
              This promise runs across the whole line. See it in practice on
              <a href="/flow/" class="text-primary hover:text-primary/80 transition-colors">Flow</a>,
              where the documents are free forever and the AI is the plan; on
              <a href="/relay/" class="text-primary hover:text-primary/80 transition-colors">Relay</a>,
              where the engine is free and open and a license only adds the packs you own; and on
              <a href="/arena/" class="text-primary hover:text-primary/80 transition-colors">Arena</a>,
              where every install writes a receipt you can read.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
